  "boundaries": [
    "Four actual original-code failures using in-memory session manager/guards and finite history; fifteen existing WS controls pass on the same original source.",
    "Original test patch uses the old guard signature; final controls carry the newly required private identity and expand positive coverage. Original source/diff/log retained.",
    "One instance identity allocation per session; detached sockets cannot affect a recreated entry. Identity does not own the broadcast sender; deletion closes that channel after any already-buffered messages.",
    "Ordinary shared-ID upsert retains identity and replaces shared filter/scope; this existing behavior is preserved, including service-to-ephemeral scope changes.",
    "History is newest-first in publication order, not an arbitrary timestamp sort. Existing chronological live arrays remain unchanged. History limit and eviction count remain unchanged.",
    "No new ingestion commit barriers, storage encoding, SQL, dependency, global budget or verified repair implementation. No benchmark or performance improvement claim.",
    "JSON-RPC envelope/filter semantics, broadcast lag, reorg notifications, dashboard ordering and integrated acceptance remain open. The shared-query resource policy remains pending."
